  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Dynamics Information Technology obligated $3.4B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. General Dynamics Information Technology won 827 awards with an average award size of $4.1M, and obligations were down 27.0% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $1B in obligations, followed by the General Services Administration with $758M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $741M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market for General Dynamics Information Technology with $1.6B obligated, followed by Custom Computer Programming Services with $576M and Engineering Services with $421M. Other notable markets include Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $160M and Other Computer Related Services at $178M. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $2.4B in FY21 to a peak of $4.8B in FY24, then fell to $4.6B in FY25 and to $3.4B in FY26. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations trended over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Obligations rose from $2.4B in FY21 to $4.1B in FY22 and to $4.3B in FY23, then increased to $4.8B in FY24. Obligations declined to $4.6B in FY25 and to $3.4B in FY26, a change recorded as down 27.0% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and which markets dominate?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $1B in obligations, followed by the General Services Administration at $758M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $741M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market at $1.6B, with Custom Computer Programming Services at $576M and Engineering Services at $421M also prominent."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does General Dynamics Information Technology make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "General Dynamics Information Technology obligated $3.4B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. General Dynamics Information Technology won 827 awards for the period with an average award size of $4.1M, and obligations were down 27.0% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from General Dynamics Information Technology?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1B. The General Services Administration obligated $758M, the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $741M, the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $161M, and other buyers include the Department of State ($137M), the Department of the Interior ($135M), the Department of Homeland Security ($128M), the Department of Transportation ($79.9M), the Department of Commerce ($54.4M), and the Environmental Protection Agency ($52.6M)."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does General Dynamics Information Technology sell to the government?",
      "a": "General Dynamics Information Technology sells Computer Systems Design Services to the government, with $1.6B obligated. Other principal offerings include Custom Computer Programming Services ($576M), Engineering Services ($421M), Other Computer Related Services ($178M), Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services ($160M), and Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services ($116M)."
    },
